Add Zoom Window panel for magnified writing

Purpose: GoodNotes-style zoom window. A box on the page is shown
magnified in a panel docked below the tabs; strokes written in the
panel land inside the box, so small handwriting stays legible while
writing. Toggle with F7 or the canvas menu.

Behaviour:
- Buttons move the box left/right, start a new line, resize it.
- Auto-advance: finishing a brush stroke in the trigger zone (right
  tenth of the box) moves the box on, keeping a quarter of the
  writing in view. The line ends at the page the box is on; the last
  step is clamped flush to the page border, the next stroke wraps.
- A new line starts at the page's left edge or where the box was
  last dragged to (toolbar choice). Return height defaults to the
  row spacing of a lines/grid background.
- On the main canvas, a first pen-down in (or just outside) the box
  drags it; the bottom-right handle drags its width, height follows
  the panel aspect.
- The main camera scrolls by the smallest shift that keeps the box in
  view; an axis where the box cannot fit follows only once the box
  has left the view entirely (no flicker).

Approach:
- Engine: ZoomWindow (crates/rnote-engine/src/zoomwindow.rs) with its
  own Camera. Panel strokes are drawn immediately with piet, because
  the store caches stroke textures for one zoom and two views would
  fight over it. The pen preview reuses the drawable code through an
  EngineView built with the panel camera.
- Input: panel events reuse canvas/input.rs through InputSurface
  (which widget positions are relative to, which engine entry point
  receives them), so backlog handling and stylus quirks stay in one
  place. Box dragging is intercepted in Engine::handle_pen_event, in
  document coordinates; panel input is never intercepted.
- Advance is armed by pen-down and consumed by the first pen-up, so
  the box never moves while the pen is down or jumps twice.
- UI: crates/rnote-ui/src/zoomwindow/. The paned splits the whole
  toolbar overlay from the panel so floating pickers stay above it.
  GTK4 reuses cached child render nodes, so the inner canvas itself
  must be queued for redraw. The panel binds the followed canvas'
  cursor.
- A hidden panel drops its background tile and does no tile work.

Constraints: stock behaviour is unchanged while the panel is hidden.
The file format is untouched. New sources must be listed in the
crates' meson.build.

